{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+, Anti-MRSA", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (48.15%) to LANTIBIOTIC Salivaricin B G: 19%, C=T=S: 11%. It shares similar ring patterns and the mersacidin-like lipid II binding motif. However, the C-terminal part of estercin A is shorter and unique. Chemical modification: three thioether bonds: T7-C12, T9-C25, and S16-C26. S18 is dehydrated. Activity: active against L. lactis MG1363 (MIC 4 ug/ml), L-onocytogenes LMG10470 (MIC > 64 ug/ml), S. aureus LMG10147 or LMG15975 MRSA (MIC 4-16 ug/ml), E. faecalis LMG16216 or LMG16003 (MIC 64 ug/ml) anti-VRE, B. ereus ATCC14579 (MIC 8 ug/ml), C. botulinum CECT551 (MIC 32 ug/ml), bowel infection-associated C. perfringens CECT376 (MIC 1 ug/ml), and C. tetani CECT4629 (MIC 4 ug/ml). Peptide stability: heat-stable at 95oC for 4 h (activity loss 30%). trypsin-resistant (no R and one C-terminal K). Antimicrobial robustness: activity retained at pH 2, 4, 7, and 10. pH-insensitive. MOA:bacteria:L. lactis MG1363: binding to lipid II inhibited peptide activity. Recombinant production:bacteria:Escherichia coli: heterologously expressed in the His-tagged form, desalted by the C18 open column.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "39814593", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "J Nat Prod. 2025 Feb 28;88(2):262-273. doi: 10.1021/acs.jnatprod.4c00814. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP05250", "source_id": "AP05250", "source_numeric_id": "05250", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP05250", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Heterologous Expression and Characterization of Estercin A, a Class II Lanthipeptide Derived from Clostridium estertheticum CF016, with Antimicr